      "rev_n_8_9aaa63_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_9aaa63_1",
        "node_id": "n_8_9aaa63",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2: To efficiently determine the number of intersecting wire pairs, we can use a combinatorial approach. For each pair of poles, calculate the slopes of the lines connecting them. If two pairs of poles form lines with the same slope, they lie on the same line and should not be counted as intersecting. Otherwise, check if the lines intersect by comparing their equations. This method reduces the need for complex geometric calculations and ensures accurate identification of intersecting pairs.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "3535506246858576827",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_8_9aaa63_0",
